WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.800
Jeremy Renner's Clint Barton has&nbsp;
remained on the sidelines of the MCU,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:08.720
but the Disney+ streaming service is&nbsp;
about to change that with "Hawkeye."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:12.640
We've set our sights on everything you'll&nbsp;
want to know about the superhero series.

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:18.640
Despite many Marvel's other Disney+ series getting&nbsp;
shuffled around due to the COVID-19 pandemic,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:22.960
it seems as though "Hawkeye" may always&nbsp;
have been destined for a holiday release.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:27.760
The six-episode season will begin its run the day&nbsp;
before Thanksgiving, with the first two episodes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:34.160
dropping on November 24, 2021. Subsequent episodes&nbsp;
will release weekly, with the finale releasing on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:39.280
December 22. That's perfect timing for the&nbsp;
holiday-themed series, which seems to follow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:43.840
Clint Barton as he fights to get home with his&nbsp;
family in time to celebrate Christmas together.

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:45.680
"Should we be worried?"

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:47.680
"I'll be home for Christmas, I promise."

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:53.040
Two-time Oscar nominee Jeremy Renner has&nbsp;
long been one of the more underutilized&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:57.520
members of the original Avengers, but that&nbsp;
will all change with "Hawkeye." His solo&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.520 --> 00:01:02.720
series will mark the first time the character&nbsp;
has ever had a central role in an MCU story.

00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:06.800
Clint Barton's only appearances outside&nbsp;
the "Avengers" movies thus far consist of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:12.080
a brief cameo in "Thor" and a supporting role in&nbsp;
"Captain America: Civil War." Renner didn't even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:17.760
appear in "Avengers: Infinity War," his absence&nbsp;
explained in a single line from Natasha Romanoff.

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:18.400
"Where's Clint?"

00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:20.400
"After the whole Accord situation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:24.240
he and Scott took a deal. It was too tough&nbsp;
on their families. They're on house arrest."

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:29.040
While Hawkeye did have a meatier role to play&nbsp;
in "Avengers: Endgame," it'll be nice to see&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:34.400
him finally take center stage. However, even&nbsp;
in his own eponymous series, he won't be alone.

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:38.800
Along with the announcement that Renner would be&nbsp;
picking up Clint Barton's bow and arrows again&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:43.360
came the exciting news that "Hawkeye" would&nbsp;
see him passing the torch to Kate Bishop.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:47.120
As fans of the "Hawkeye" comics are&nbsp;
well aware, Kate is Barton's protege&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:51.760
who takes up the Hawkeye mantle herself. She is&nbsp;
eventually given Barton's bow to use as her own.

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:56.480
"What I get to do ultimately in&nbsp;
the show is shepherd an amazing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.200 --> 00:02:00.560
character to be, ultimately,&nbsp;
probably a better version of me."

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:05.120
"Hawkeye" will draw inspiration from the&nbsp;
recent comics run from writer Matt Fraction&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.120 --> 00:02:10.160
and artist David Aja, in which Bishop is&nbsp;
Barton's occasional partner in fighting crime.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.160 --> 00:02:14.560
The character in the comics is young,&nbsp;
strong-willed, and doesn't shy away from danger.

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:19.440
In Marvel Studios' "Hawkeye," Kate Bishop will&nbsp;
be played by Hailee Steinfeld. The actress was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:24.160
confirmed in the role in late 2020 after being&nbsp;
rumored for the role of Kate for more than a year.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:26.960
Speaking to Collider about her&nbsp;
involvement, Steinfeld said,

00:02:26.960 --> 00:02:31.360
"I'm just so honored to be a part of the MCU&nbsp;
... It's been a wonderful experience, developing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.360 --> 00:02:36.160
this character and taking elements of her from&nbsp;
the comics and what we know with her history."

00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:40.800
"Hawkeye" is Steinfeld's first live-action&nbsp;
superhero role. However, she's no stranger&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:45.680
to the genre or to Marvel's expansive roster&nbsp;
of characters, having voiced Spider-Gwen in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:50.800
the Oscar-winning animated film "Spider-Man: Into&nbsp;
the Spider-Verse." Additionally, Steinfeld also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:55.520
already has her own Oscar nomination under her&nbsp;
belt for her role in the Coen Brothers' 2010&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.520 --> 00:03:00.880
remake of "True Grit." In the film, which was&nbsp;
also her feature film debut, she starred as the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:07.120
determined Mattie Ross alongside Matt Damon, Jeff&nbsp;
Bridges, and eventual MCU villain Josh Brolin.

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:11.710
Considering Steinfeld's impressive resume,&nbsp;
she seems more than capable of going toe to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.710 --> 00:03:16.160
toe — or perhaps we should say, bow to&nbsp;
bow — with Jeremy Renner in "Hawkeye."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.160 --> 00:03:20.000
And who knows, depending on what happens&nbsp;
in "Hawkeye," it's possible Kate Bishop&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:24.000
could go on to play an even bigger part&nbsp;
in the MCU than Clint Barton ever did.

00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:28.400
Jeremy Renner isn't the only Marvel&nbsp;
actor set to return in "Hawkeye."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:34.400
Ben Sakamoto, Ava Russo, and Cade Woodward will&nbsp;
be reprising their roles as Barton's children&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:39.280
Cooper, Lila, and Nathaniel Barton, who were&nbsp;
last seen at the end of "Avengers: Endgame."

00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:43.200
While Clint Barton was the opposite of&nbsp;
a family man in Matt Fraction's comics,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:47.680
the Barton family has been a huge part&nbsp;
of Hawkeye's characterization in the MCU.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:51.760
His grief over their loss in "the Blip"&nbsp;
functioned as his motivation for becoming the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.760 --> 00:03:56.240
assassin Ronin at the beginning of "Avengers:&nbsp;
Endgame." Later, the possibility of getting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.240 --> 00:04:00.640
them back served as Barton's incentive to&nbsp;
rejoin the Avengers on their time heist.

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:04.960
Emmy nominee Linda Cardellini will also&nbsp;
be reprising her role from the MCU films&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.960 --> 00:04:09.520
as Clint's wife Laura. Cardellini has most&nbsp;
recently been co-starring with Christina&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.520 --> 00:04:14.480
Applegate in the Netflix series "Dead to Me,"&nbsp;
which has a third and final season forthcoming.

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:18.880
Although we don't yet know how big a role Laura&nbsp;
Barton will play in "Hawkeye," trailers have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:22.640
confirmed that the Bartons' marriage still&nbsp;
appears to be in decent shape — assuming,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.640 --> 00:04:25.120
of course, that Clint can make&nbsp;
it home in time for Christmas.

00:04:25.840 --> 00:04:29.760
Jeremy Renner and Hailee Steinfeld may be&nbsp;
sharing top billing as the lead characters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.760 --> 00:04:33.760
of "Hawkeye," but they're far from the&nbsp;
only serious acting talent in the series.

00:04:33.760 --> 00:04:39.120
Oscar-nominee and "The Conjuring" series co-star&nbsp;
Vera Farmiga has been cast as Kate Bishop's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.120 --> 00:04:44.480
mother Eleanor, while Tony Dalton is slated to&nbsp;
play Jack Duquesne, also known as Swordsman,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.480 --> 00:04:49.360
one of Clint Barton's mentors. Duqusne has had&nbsp;
both heroic and villainous arcs in the comics,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.360 --> 00:04:52.880
so it will be interesting to see in&nbsp;
what direction the series takes him.

00:04:52.880 --> 00:04:58.880
"Hawkeye" will also serve as the live-action debut&nbsp;
of Maya Lopez, who adopts the superhero name Echo.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.880 --> 00:05:03.840
In the comics, Maya is a deaf Native American&nbsp;
woman who has the power to perfectly mimic human&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.840 --> 00:05:08.960
movements, giving her the ability to quickly adapt&nbsp;
to a wide variety of skills and combat styles.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.960 --> 00:05:14.720
She'll be played by deaf actor Alaqua Cox,&nbsp;
who is from the Menominee and Mohican nations.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.720 --> 00:05:19.040
"Hawkeye" will serve as Cox's screen debut,&nbsp;
but Marvel Studios seems to already have a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.040 --> 00:05:24.560
lot of faith in her; the studio is already moving&nbsp;
ahead with development on Echo's own solo series.

00:05:24.560 --> 00:05:30.000
Maya's father William will be played by veteran&nbsp;
actor Zahn McClarnon, who you may recognize from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:35.200
"Westworld" and "Longmire." The Lopez family&nbsp;
has a deep history in the world of the comics,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:40.800
with Echo's storylines closely intertwining with&nbsp;
characters such as Daredevil and Moon Knight.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.800 --> 00:05:44.720
It remains to be seen if she and William&nbsp;
will play a significant role in "Hawkeye,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.720 --> 00:05:48.640
or if their appearances will serve as more&nbsp;
of a set up to Echo's eventual spin-off.

00:05:49.280 --> 00:05:54.400
On the villain side of things, Florence Pugh will&nbsp;
also be appearing in "Hawkeye" as Yelena Belova,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.400 --> 00:05:59.040
sister of Clint's dearly departed bestie,&nbsp;
Natasha Romanoff. The Oscar-nominated actor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.040 --> 00:06:03.280
recently had a huge MCU breakout moment&nbsp;
in "Black Widow," in which the two women&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.280 --> 00:06:07.440
teamed up to take down the man responsible&nbsp;
for their abusive training in the Red Room.

00:06:07.440 --> 00:06:11.840
However, while Yelena largely acted as a&nbsp;
hero in the film, things take a turn in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.840 --> 00:06:16.160
"Black Widow"'s post-credit scene. The scene&nbsp;
finds Yelena mourning Natasha's death at her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.160 --> 00:06:21.040
sister's gravesite when she's approached&nbsp;
by Contessa Valentina Allegra de Fontaine,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.040 --> 00:06:25.520
who was introduced in "The Falcon and the Winter&nbsp;
Soldier" as one of the newer behind-the-scenes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.520 --> 00:06:30.320
power players of the MCU. The Contessa tells&nbsp;
Yelena that she has a new target for her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.320 --> 00:06:32.560
paving the way for her appearance in "Hawkeye."

00:06:33.280 --> 00:06:38.000
"Maybe you'd like a shot at the man&nbsp;
responsible for your sister's death."

00:06:38.640 --> 00:06:43.680
But Yelena won't be the only character blocking&nbsp;
Clint's path to a festive family Christmas.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:43.680 --> 00:06:48.000
Irish actor Fra Fee has been cast as a&nbsp;
villainous character referred to in the show&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:52.640
as Kazi. In a Tweet around the time of his&nbsp;
casting announcement, Fee indicated that Kazi&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:52.640 --> 00:06:57.760
will be a live-action take on Kazimierz&nbsp;
Kazimierczak, also known as The Clown.

00:06:57.760 --> 00:07:02.080
And of course, then there's the Tracksuit&nbsp;
Draculas. The primary antagonists in Matt&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.080 --> 00:07:06.880
Fraction's "Hawkeye" comics are members of the&nbsp;
Russian mafia, whom Clint dubs the "Tracksuit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.880 --> 00:07:12.080
Draculas," due to their heavy accents and their&nbsp;
affinity for wearing velour tracksuits. These&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.080 --> 00:07:17.760
Russian mobsters have an extremely limited English&nbsp;
vocabulary, relying heavily on the words "bro" and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.760 --> 00:07:22.480
"seriously" to convey the bulk of their meaning.&nbsp;
They drive much of the small-scale conflict of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.480 --> 00:07:26.880
Fraction's comics, which tend to center on&nbsp;
the tenants of Barton's apartment building.

00:07:26.880 --> 00:07:30.640
Trailers have confirmed that the Tracksuit&nbsp;
Draculas will be teaming up to take down&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.640 --> 00:07:35.120
Clint Barton. The trailer also gives us&nbsp;
a glimpse of boxer-turned-actor Aleks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:35.120 --> 00:07:40.960
Paunovic playing a character who seems to be Ivan&nbsp;
Banionis, the leader of the Tracksuit Draculas.

00:07:40.960 --> 00:07:45.120
Considering the Tracksuit Draculas storyline&nbsp;
from the comics is very tied up with Barton's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:45.120 --> 00:07:49.920
characterization as a single, childless guy&nbsp;
living in New York City, there will no doubt be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.920 --> 00:07:54.240
some changes to how the villains are portrayed&nbsp;
in the Disney+ series. But, seriously bro,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:54.240 --> 00:07:58.400
no matter how they wind up on the wrong side of&nbsp;
Clint's trick arrows, we're happy to see them.

00:07:58.400 --> 00:08:02.880
Between taking on the many villains of New York&nbsp;
City and the vengeance-seeking sister of one of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.880 --> 00:08:08.160
his closest friends, one thing is certain: Clint&nbsp;
will have his hands full this holiday season.

00:08:08.960 --> 00:08:12.960
Fraction's "Hawkeye" comics feature a&nbsp;
wide assortment of interesting characters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:12.960 --> 00:08:17.760
any one of whom would make a welcome addition&nbsp;
to the MCU. Possible allies for Clint and Kate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.760 --> 00:08:21.440
include Clint's brother, Barney Barton;&nbsp;
Clint's friend and neighbor, Grills;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:21.440 --> 00:08:26.480
or Penny, the ex-wife of one of the Tracksuit&nbsp;
Draculas. Bobbi Morse, also known as Mockingbird,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.480 --> 00:08:31.120
and Jessica Drew, also known as Spider-Woman,&nbsp;
also appear in the Hawkeye comics. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:31.120 --> 00:08:35.760
since the MCU version of Clint is happily married,&nbsp;
their roles as Clint's ex-wife and current&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:35.760 --> 00:08:40.160
girlfriend, respectively, would likely have to&nbsp;
be rewritten for the show if they were to appear.

00:08:40.160 --> 00:08:44.400
The character of Bobbi Morse has already appeared&nbsp;
on the TV show "Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D.," where&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.400 --> 00:08:49.840
she was portrayed by Adrianne Palicki. However,&nbsp;
FandomWire reports that Palicki won't be reprising&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:49.840 --> 00:08:55.280
her role for "Hawkeye," and that the character&nbsp;
will be recast. Similarly, speculation is swirling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:55.280 --> 00:08:59.760
among MCU fans that the character "Game of&nbsp;
Thrones" star Emilia Clarke will be playing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:59.760 --> 00:09:04.720
in the upcoming "Secret Invasion" series is in&nbsp;
fact Jessica Drew. If that turns out to be true,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:04.720 --> 00:09:08.400
could the character make her first appearance&nbsp;
in "Hawkeye"? Who knows, but it wouldn't be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:08.400 --> 00:09:12.480
the first time Marvel has thrown a surprise&nbsp;
character introduction into one of their shows.

00:09:12.480 --> 00:09:17.200
Speaking of MCU tie-ins, in one issue of&nbsp;
Fraction's "Hawkeye," Clint briefly teams up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.200 --> 00:09:22.960
with Wolverine and Spider-Man to battle members&nbsp;
of Advanced Idea Mechanics. Otherwise known as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.960 --> 00:09:27.440
A.I.M., the group is an organization of evil&nbsp;
scientists that serve as one of the various&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.440 --> 00:09:32.160
villainous groups in the Marvel Universe. However,&nbsp;
it's only a minor subplot, and the "Hawkeye"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:32.160 --> 00:09:36.800
series could easily nod to it while swapping out&nbsp;
most of the details. Not only could "Hawkeye"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:36.800 --> 00:09:41.120
substitute some different villains since A.I.M.&nbsp;
was last seen in "Iron Man 3," but the series&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:41.120 --> 00:09:46.080
could also pull in a totally different pair of&nbsp;
Avengers. Possibly some avengers with closer ties&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:46.080 --> 00:09:51.520
to Clint than Spider-Man or Wolverine, especially&nbsp;
since the latter still hasn't made his MCU debut.

00:09:51.520 --> 00:09:56.080
Perhaps instead, Clint might team up with&nbsp;
Wanda Maximoff, with whom he already has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:56.080 --> 00:09:59.760
somewhat of a mentoring relationship.&nbsp;
Other candidates could include Clint's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:59.760 --> 00:10:05.200
former S.H.I.E.L.D. colleagues like Nick Fury&nbsp;
and Maria Hill, or Sam Wilson and Bucky Barnes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:05.200 --> 00:10:08.960
Even someone like Scott Lang could make sense,&nbsp;
especially if his daughter Cassie shows up.

00:10:08.960 --> 00:10:12.640
In the Matt Fraction comics, Kate Bishop is&nbsp;
already a former member of the superhero team&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:12.640 --> 00:10:17.040
Young Avengers. However, considering the&nbsp;
Young Avengers don't yet exist in the MCU,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:17.040 --> 00:10:22.400
it may make more sense for "Hawkeye" to be the&nbsp;
property that sets up their eventual introduction.

00:10:22.400 --> 00:10:27.200
Kate isn't the first potential Young Avenger to&nbsp;
enter the MCU. The first was Ant-Man's daughter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:27.200 --> 00:10:31.760
Cassie Lang, who aged into a teenager&nbsp;
during the time jump in "Avengers: Endgame."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:31.760 --> 00:10:36.400
In the comics, Cassie follows in her father's&nbsp;
footsteps by using Pym particles to become the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:36.400 --> 00:10:40.960
size-altering superhero Stature, and is&nbsp;
close friends with Kate Bishop's Hawkeye.

00:10:40.960 --> 00:10:46.160
Cassie has since been followed by Billy and&nbsp;
Tommy, the twin sons of Wanda Maximoff and Vision.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:46.160 --> 00:10:49.840
While the brothers disappeared along with&nbsp;
the rest of Wanda's conjured world at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:49.840 --> 00:10:59.840
end of "WandaVision," they reappeared as spectral&nbsp;
voices during the post-credit scene in the finale.

00:10:59.840 --> 00:11:02.720
"Mom, help please"

00:11:02.720 --> 00:11:07.360
In the comics, Billy and Tommy grow up to&nbsp;
be the Young Avengers Wiccan and Speed.

00:11:07.360 --> 00:11:12.800
In "The Falcon and the Winter Soldier," we briefly&nbsp;
met Elijah Bradley, grandson of Isaiah Bradley,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:12.800 --> 00:11:18.080
the Black Captain America. In the comics, Elijah&nbsp;
takes up the mantle of the Young Avenger known as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:18.080 --> 00:11:21.840
Patriot. And "Loki" introduced us&nbsp;
to the character of Young Loki,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:21.840 --> 00:11:26.080
a variant form of the character who is also&nbsp;
part of the Young Avengers team in the comics.

00:11:26.080 --> 00:11:30.400
With nearly the entire Young Avengers&nbsp;
roster already established in the MCU,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:30.400 --> 00:11:34.640
we wouldn't be surprised if "Hawkeye" finally&nbsp;
lays the groundwork for the team to come together.

00:11:35.280 --> 00:11:39.280
Arguably one of the best parts of&nbsp;
Fraction's "Hawkeye" run is Clint's dog,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:39.280 --> 00:11:43.840
Lucky. The two are introduced when Clint saves&nbsp;
the pooch from one of the Tracksuit Draculas,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:43.840 --> 00:11:48.240
and then adopts him. While his tag&nbsp;
reads "Arrow," Clint renames him Lucky.

00:11:48.240 --> 00:11:52.560
Clint's canine companion will be played&nbsp;
by a golden retriever named Jolt, and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:52.560 --> 00:11:57.440
character's inclusion in the series opens up a&nbsp;
wide range of story possibilities. In the comics,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:57.440 --> 00:12:02.000
he even partakes in a few adventures of his&nbsp;
own. He accompanies Kate when she moves to L.A.,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:02.000 --> 00:12:05.760
helps Clint track down Tracksuit&nbsp;
Draculas, and even gets shot at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:05.760 --> 00:12:09.840
one point. If the series goes this route,&nbsp;
don't worry — Lucky recovers just fine.

00:12:10.720 --> 00:12:15.520
Serving as writer and executive producer&nbsp;
for "Hawkeye" is Jonathan Igla. While Igla&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:15.520 --> 00:12:20.480
has produced several other shows, including the&nbsp;
short-lived but critically beloved series "Pitch,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:20.480 --> 00:12:25.200
he's best known for his work on AMC's juggernaut&nbsp;
series "Mad Men," where he served as a writer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:25.200 --> 00:12:30.720
and executive story editor. Although Igla's resume&nbsp;
doesn't boast much experience with the high-octane&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:30.720 --> 00:12:35.840
action the MCU is known for, his style may be&nbsp;
perfect for the more character-driven "Hawkeye."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:35.840 --> 00:12:40.720
After all, "Mad Men" was widely celebrated for&nbsp;
its outstanding characters, snappy dialogue,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:40.720 --> 00:12:45.440
and strong storytelling, three elements that&nbsp;
also stood out in Matt Fraction's "Hawkeye" run.

00:12:45.440 --> 00:12:49.360
Fraction's "Hawkeye" storylines tended&nbsp;
to revolve around the question of what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:49.360 --> 00:12:51.840
a superhero does when he's not being a superhero.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:52.400 --> 00:12:57.360
While Fraction's run did have its fair share of&nbsp;
bad guys and sinister plots, each issue tended&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:57.360 --> 00:13:02.960
to focus less on Clint Barton's extraordinary&nbsp;
abilities and more on his regular day-to-day life.

00:13:02.960 --> 00:13:05.760
Of course, we also expect plenty of MCU superhero&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:05.760 --> 00:13:09.920
action from "Hawkeye." But if the series&nbsp;
is using Fraction's comics as a roadmap,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:09.920 --> 00:13:15.120
we can expect for it to be focused on small-scale&nbsp;
personal conflicts and character relationships&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:15.120 --> 00:13:20.480
far more than hugely powerful supervillains,&nbsp;
making Igla the perfect choice to helm the series.

00:13:21.040 --> 00:13:25.280
After being blissfully absent for all of&nbsp;
"Avengers: Infinity War," Clint Barton&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:25.280 --> 00:13:30.480
had a rough time during "Avengers: Endgame." The&nbsp;
film opened with Barton's wife and three children&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:30.480 --> 00:13:35.840
turning to dust before his eyes, following the&nbsp;
Avengers' failure to stop Thanos in "Infinity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:35.840 --> 00:13:40.640
War." The next time we saw him after the film's&nbsp;
five-year time jump, he had left the superhero&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:40.640 --> 00:13:46.240
mantle of Hawkeye behind, and had become the&nbsp;
ruthless vigilante known as Ronin. His best friend&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:46.240 --> 00:13:51.600
Natasha eventually tracks him down in Japan after&nbsp;
he has just murdered a street full of Yakuza,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:51.600 --> 00:13:55.760
offering him hope with their plan for the&nbsp;
time heist. But while Clint is ultimately&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:55.760 --> 00:14:00.400
able to get his family back by the end of the&nbsp;
movie, it's at the cost of Natasha's life.

00:14:00.400 --> 00:14:04.320
With the "Hawkeye" series confirmed to&nbsp;
take place after the events of "Endgame,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:04.320 --> 00:14:09.360
that leaves a lot for Clint to be reckoning&nbsp;
with the next time we see him. Not only will he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:09.360 --> 00:14:14.160
likely still be mourning the loss of Natasha,&nbsp;
whose death he tried and failed to prevent,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:14.160 --> 00:14:19.280
but he'll also have to face the horrible things&nbsp;
he did as Ronin. That's not even to mention that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:19.280 --> 00:14:24.480
he'll have super-spy Yelena after him, seeking&nbsp;
retribution for Natasha's death. Additionally,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:24.480 --> 00:14:28.400
we can probably expect to see how the Barton&nbsp;
family is coping with the aftermath of "the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:28.400 --> 00:14:33.680
Blip," since coming back after five years&nbsp;
as dust is sure to be a sizeable adjustment.

00:14:33.680 --> 00:14:38.240
Trailers for "Hawkeye" see the superhero&nbsp;
taking his kids on a fun trip to New York City,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:38.240 --> 00:14:42.880
but of course, those plans quickly go sideways.&nbsp;
The trailers indicate that the main plot of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:42.880 --> 00:14:47.040
"Hawkeye" will revolve around Clint getting&nbsp;
stuck in New York City away from his family&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:47.040 --> 00:14:51.600
before Christmas, battling bad guys that&nbsp;
are somehow tied to his days as Ronin.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:51.600 --> 00:14:56.160
Complicating matters is that it appears the&nbsp;
entire New York underworld is after Clint,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:56.160 --> 00:15:00.560
while he lacks the superhuman strength and&nbsp;
resilience of his extraordinary teammates.

00:15:00.560 --> 00:15:04.960
Of course, Hawkeye's lack of superpowers&nbsp;
has always been a running gag in the MCU.

00:15:04.960 --> 00:15:07.680
"The city is flying, we're&nbsp;
fighting an army of robots,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:09.120 --> 00:15:12.000
and I have a bow and arrow.&nbsp;
None of this makes sense."

00:15:12.000 --> 00:15:16.640
But for Clint, being a hero has always&nbsp;
been more about a mindset than superpowers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:16.640 --> 00:15:20.160
and it seems that theme will&nbsp;
carry over to his solo series.

00:15:20.160 --> 00:15:23.440
It seems likely that despite the&nbsp;
Tracksuit Draculas and many other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:23.440 --> 00:15:27.360
villains threatening Clint, the main focus&nbsp;
of the "Hawkeye" series will be on Clint&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:27.360 --> 00:15:31.760
training Kate to eventually take over for&nbsp;
him. Teaching Kate that she doesn't need&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:31.760 --> 00:15:35.520
powers in order to accomplish great things&nbsp;
would be in line with Fraction's comics,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:35.520 --> 00:15:40.720
which are much more interested in Clint's&nbsp;
everyday attitude than in his enhanced skillset.

00:15:40.720 --> 00:15:43.280
"You want to be a superhero?&nbsp;
You put your life in danger."

00:15:43.280 --> 00:15:46.880
Keeping with the theme of focusing&nbsp;
on Hawkeye's most human qualities,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:46.880 --> 00:15:51.440
Renner has confirmed that Barton's hearing loss&nbsp;
will play a factor in "Hawkeye," as it did in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:51.440 --> 00:15:56.080
Fraction's comics. Considering we know that Echo&nbsp;
will be appearing in the series, we wouldn't be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:56.080 --> 00:16:00.960
surprised if hearing loss and deafness turn&nbsp;
out to be a significant part of "Hawkeye."

00:16:00.960 --> 00:16:04.960
Will Clint and Kate be able to take on the&nbsp;
Tracksuit Draculas and other various Marvel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:04.960 --> 00:16:08.880
baddies in time for Clint to make it home&nbsp;
for Christmas on the farm with his family?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:08.880 --> 00:16:13.440
And will Clint finally retire for good&nbsp;
and pass the mantle to his young protege?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:13.440 --> 00:16:19.760
We'll find out when the first two episodes of&nbsp;
"Hawkeye" shoot onto Disney+ on November 24, 2021.

00:16:19.760 --> 00:16:21.600
"It's gonna be the best Christmas ever."

